0033:     - The marker-to-marker offset has both row and column components, with unequal magnitudes.
0034: 
0035:     Rule
0036:     - Decompose the vector between markers into a 45-degree diagonal vector plus the remaining horizontal/vertical vector.
0037:     - Treat those two vectors as adjacent sides of a parallelogram, with the markers as opposite corners.
0038:     - Paint the four sides green while preserving the marker pixels.
0039: 
0040:     Key insight
0041:     - The outline is not a direct line interpolation; it is the perimeter of the parallelogram induced by the diagonal and axis-aligned parts of the marker offset.
0042:     """
